cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use percent-nlu, please cite it as below."
title: "percent-nlu: a tiny on-device model for natural-language percentage questions"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Emanoel S. Vieira"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-02"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/EmanoelV/percent-nlu"
url: "https://huggingface.co/EmanoelV/percent-nlu"
keywords:
  - percentage calculator
  - natural language understanding
  - tiny model
  - on-device
  - tool calling
  - English
  - Portuguese
  - Spanish
abstract: >-
  percent-nlu is a 1.16M-parameter Transformer that reads percentage questions written in English,
  Portuguese or Spanish and returns the matching calculator tool call (percent_of, what_percent, percent_increase,
  percent_decrease, apply_increase, apply_decrease) with each number in its role. It runs in the browser
  (1.2 MB int8, dependency-free JavaScript) in about a millisecond.
